    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0550" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.428/453</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spring Rice</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 519</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note No. 1889 of November 13, the substance of which I have
                    communicated to the Canadian Government.</p>
                <p>With reference to the last paragraph thereof, I have the honour to inform you
                    that it is my understanding also that the representatives of the two countries
                    are only to be empowered to come to a mutually satisfactory understanding as to
                    all pending questions, and to report the result of their deliberations to their
                    respective Governments as a basis for the subsequent negotiation of a formal
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
